# JayLexi 0.1 and 0.2 on a wide MiniRumble sample (docs/kitlab.md, docs/bench/kitlab-0.2-arms.md).
# The cloud reads 0.2 (second-wave surfing) at about +0.3 over 0.1 on two 48-bot samples; this card
# reads both released jars, and Komarious 1.88 as the reference, on 112 bots (top 12 by name and 100
# rank bands, seed 3: kitlab/mini-wide-field.txt), so the projection for 5th (WeeksOnEnd 87.35 live)
# rests on more of the division. JayLexi 0.1 is live 6th at 86.95.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-jaylexi-w1        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-jaylexi-w1)
# Run it from master:
#   git checkout master && git pull
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned (--parallel auto: the host profile's width). Every step
# resumes; no step needs a decision. Nothing here touches Hadur or the other small bots.
#
# RERUN 2026-10-29 (issue #433): the first w1-KOM failed with 6 failed battles, Komarious facing its own
# jar. It now runs on kitlab/mini-wide-ref-field.txt (the field less Komarious) under the label KOM2;
# J01 and J02 are done and are not rerun. Rerun with the same command; only w1-KOM, read and pr run.
#
# Arms, each a released jar fetched from its GitHub release:
#   J01   JayLexi 0.1 (control)   J02   JayLexi 0.2   KOM   Komarious 1.88 (reference, live 87.54)
# 112 bots x 6 seeds = 672 battles an arm, 35 rounds each; about 20 min an arm on the PC, about 1 h
# in all.
# Read: J02 against J01 on the same battles' opponents (the paired gain), and each against KOM for a
# predicted APS. 0.2 holds when its gain's low end is above zero.
# Stop rules on every step (docs/bench/watch.md; halt, every battle fought is kept and a rerun
# resumes): 20 failed battles (a broken jar), no battle in 30 minutes (a hung step), or 40+ skipped
# turns a battle over the last 100 (the PR #331 build-up). A halt at worst leaves the rest of that
# arm and the arms after it unrun, at most 2,016 battles (about 1 h). No early finish on score:
# each step is one robot. ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on a stop.

set MVN = mvn -q -Drobocode.version=1.11.1 compile exec:java
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin
set REL = https://github.com/lgriffin/Hadur_Robot/releases/download

prep | ./fetch-opponents.sh --set kitlab/mini-wide-field.txt && curl -fsSL -o opponents/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.1.jar ${REL}/jaylexi-v0.1/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.1.jar && curl -fsSL -o opponents/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.2.jar ${REL}/jaylexi-v0.2/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.2.jar && bash kitlab/args.sh mini-wide opponents/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.1.jar "hadur117.mini.JayLexi 0.1" w1-J01 6 && bash kitlab/args.sh mini-wide opponents/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.2.jar "hadur117.mini.JayLexi 0.2" w1-J02 6 && bash kitlab/args.sh mini-wide opponents/voidious.mini.Komarious_1.88.jar "voidious.mini.Komarious 1.88" w1-KOM 6

w1-J01 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/kitlab-w1-J01.args"
  after: prep
  watch: battles=672
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

w1-J02 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/kitlab-w1-J02.args"
  after: w1-J01
  watch: battles=672
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

w1-KOM | bash kitlab/args.sh mini-wide-ref opponents/voidious.mini.Komarious_1.88.jar "voidious.mini.Komarious 1.88" w1-KOM2 6 && ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@work/kitlab-w1-KOM2.args"
  after: w1-J02
  watch: battles=672
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

read | (echo "# JayLexi 0.1 and 0.2 on the wide MiniRumble sample (pc-jaylexi-w1)" && echo && echo '## 0.2 against 0.1' && echo '```' && python3 tools/kitlab_read.py kitlab/mini-wide-field.txt work/kitlab-w1-J02 --ref work/kitlab-w1-J01 && echo '```' && echo && echo '## 0.2 against Komarious 1.88 (live 87.54)' && echo '```' && python3 tools/kitlab_read.py kitlab/mini-wide-field.txt work/kitlab-w1-J02 --ref work/kitlab-w1-KOM2 --ref-aps 87.54 && echo '```' && echo && echo '## 0.1 against Komarious 1.88 (live 87.54)' && echo '```' && python3 tools/kitlab_read.py kitlab/mini-wide-field.txt work/kitlab-w1-J01 --ref work/kitlab-w1-KOM2 --ref-aps 87.54 && echo '```') > ${OUT}/jaylexi-w1.md
  after: w1-KOM

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-jaylexi-w1-results "JayLexi 0.1 and 0.2 on the wide MiniRumble sample" ${OUT}/jaylexi-w1.md
  after: read
